oney  they had been pumping into afghanistan  for 20 years on which the economy had  come to totally rely  75 percent of the government's budget  disappeared overnight the world bank  halted funding that supported the  education sector and two-thirds of the  country's health centers  then  sanctions that were placed on the  taliban were applied to the new afghan  government as it was taking power  exiling the country from the  international economy  and the last part of it was the most  devastating of all  the american government decided to  freeze afghanistan's central bank  holdings  nearly 10 billion dollars that belonged  to the afghan people  what happens when you confiscate the  financial reserves of an impoverished  country  inflation spikes making food  unaffordable for millions  businesses close down and banks can't  function cutting access to income for  afghan working families  eventually the entire financial system  collapses  and that is exactly what is happening  the afghan economy is collapsing in  rapid fashion  experts say it is one of the fastest  economic contractions in recorded  history  in just a few months one of the poorest  countries in the world is facing a  faster economic decline than the u.s saw  over years during the great depression  the united states and its allies had  built an afghan economy totally  dependent on their resources and aid  and then  they cut that taking it away overnight  and on top of that  confiscated all of the country's central  bank reserves  today the jobs that the occupation had  provided are gone  afghans with bank accounts can only  access a small portion of their money  all this in the middle of a global  pandemic  and while they're experiencing their  worst drought in 35 years  afghans have been plunged into a new  level of desperation  in the unequivocal words of dr paul  spiegel professor of public health at  johns hopkins  returning from a visit to afghanistan  i can clearly state that if the united  states and other western governments do  not change their afghanistan sanction  policies  more afghans will die from sanctions  than at the hands of the taliban  ultimately  only the u.s government wields the power  to alleviate this crisis  the united states says that it cares  about afghanistan  america supplies more aid to afghanistan  than any other country  but these donations do not come close to  offsetting the damage that u.s policy is  causing the afghan people by crippling  their entire society people monitoring  the situation are clear that aid alone  will not create a stable economy  and that afghanistan needs to have  commerce and a functioning banking  system after 43 years of conflict  afghans deserve to rebuild their lives  they deserve post-conflict  reconstruction and to build a  sustainable economy that is connected to  the world  instead we're holding them back and  making them remain dependent on aid  not only is this not right  but it is not in america's best interest  in the words of the president of the  international rescue committee a charity  working in afghanistan the economy is  not just in free fall it's being  strangled  we want to say loud and clear that you  can't solve this problem of mass  malnutrition only with a humanitarian  effort  jan egeland the head of the norwegian  refugee council says it is now  paradoxically the western sanctions that  is our main problem in saving lives in  afghanistan  this policy can be ended at any time  officials within the biden  administration could protect millions of  afghans from starvation and death  the afghan people's hopes lie with  officials like national security adviser  jake sullivan  deputy treasury secretary wally adeyemo  and of course president joe biden  himself  they can end this policy right now  unfreeze the central bank reserves and  allow the afghan people to recover from  decades of war  these officials understand the value of  helping working families  of protecting our children  and ensuring that they are given the  opportunity to survive  but we need them to see  that afghanistan's children  are just as deserving of life  as children in america  the best way to address this tragedy to  stop the wave of starvation and death  is to end the sanctions we have placed  on the country  and give back the money that we have  seized  the afghan central bank was designed by  americans and the taliban have not  changed the law  as experts have pointed out it is an  independent and technocratic institution  with transparent financial flows i  appeal to you to listen to act  let's not cause an entire nation to  experience extreme harm under our watch  america's leaders can stop this but they  must act as quickly as possible  let's end these harmful sanctions let's  accept  that the war is over  i'm masuda sultan from unfreeze  afghanistan for the gravel institute  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  you

